From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Feb 16 16:01:56 2001
From: C.Schwabl () mobilkom ! at
Date: Fri, 16 Feb 2001 16:01:56 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to hot-swap disks with an MA6000/HSG60
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98233940516138

Great and fast responses as always...

Here is what i will be doing:
1) Delete the failed disk
HSG60> delete failedset disk20500

2) 
HSG60> set raid2 nopolicy

3) Remove the faulty drive with the new one...

4) Init the new disk to ensure no metadata is on it:
HSG60> init disk20500

5) Put the new disk into the raidset:
HSG60> set raid2 replace=disk20500

6) 
HSG60> set raid2 policy=best_performance

That should do it...

Thanks go to:
Timothy Brown and Bill Boddy

