From: bac <bac20000 () yahoo ! com>
Date: Thu, 15 Feb 2001 04:37:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: KZPCM-DA SCSI CARD/XP1000
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98221195604794

THE QUESTION WAS:

> I had noticed that the KZPCM-DA dual channel
> SCSI/network card is not supported under Tru64Unix
> on
> the XP1000..
> Is there any way to get this to work?? 
> 
Many thanks as usual to Alan and Dr. Blinn for
responding with excellent suggestions. 

The problem turned out to be the following:
On an AlphaStation XP1000, the KZPCM-DA only works in
PCI slot 0 for some reason. I just moved the
Powerstorm 350 into the next slot and put the KZPCM-DA
in slot 0. I am very relieved, needless to say, now i
can use my external drives. 

Thanks
Ashok



