The recent poll regarding job posting on the list shows that most
people support the idea, especially with some form of administrative
control. (The tally was 88 for, 55 against.) I've decided to give the
idea a try. During this trial run, job postings *must* be sent to me,
not the list. I'll either approve them or reject them. Once approved,
I'll post them to the list. If I get more than one per day, I'll
combine them into a single message to the list.

Attached is the first job posting.

Dave Sill
Tru64-UNIX-Managers list owner

----

From: "Thomas, Julie" <jthomas@ercot.com>

ERCOT is the Electric Reliability Council of Texas. We are the
Independent Service Operator (ISO) for the state of Texas.

We're looking for a Tru64/NT admin, i.e., a Tru64 admin with some NT
experience or an NT admin with Tru64 experience. This is a mission
critical position. This person and I will be responsible for the
computers (4xGS160, 2xES40, associated NT boxes and peripherals) that
will be controlling the power grid for the state of Texas. High
stress, but IMHO, very cool.  The position will be located at the
Austin failover site, with some travel necessary to the primary site
in the nearby thriving metropolis of Taylor (~25 miles away).  Since
this position is located at the corporate HQ, ability to deal
effectively with with executive officers would be a bonus.
Availability is ASAP; relocation and benefits are excellent. If you're
interested, please e-mail a resume to Cindy Adams,
mailto:cadams@ercot.com. If you know someone who might be interested,
please pass this along.

Questions? Feel free to e-mail me directly
mailto:jthomas@ercot.com. Here are the details:

Position Title: Compaq Tru64 UNIX/NT System Administrator

General Overview of the Position: 
Support all levels of Tru64 and NT administration
Administer the technical environment in support of the In-Scope
Applications (event-driven, real-time)
Software and hardware maintenance
Systems planning
Performance monitoring and turning
Interfaces and reporting architectures
System security
Backup management
Troubleshooting and problem determination
Scripting
Account and directory maintenance

Functional Responsibilities:
Maintain servers, external disk, and tape management systems
Upgrade operating system
Install patches/fixes provided by vendor
Assist in supporting portal, web servers, external disk, and tape
management systems
Keep servers available to user communities through proactive
management
Coordinate services with all supporting organizations and 3rd parties
Review all scope change requests for impact to the environment
Load testing 
Capacity planning and hardware selection
Disaster recovery planning
Monitor and report site availability and
performance

Professional Responsibilities:
Develop and sustain a high level understanding of the competitive
energy markets
Increase and maintain proficiency as an "Industry
Expert" on TRU64 technology, methodologies, and concepts as
appropriate (will cross-train with AIX and HP-UX)
Establish strong working relationships with key staff members in ERCOT
departments
Facilitate communications throughout the ERCOT
Develop and maintain a high level of computer skills in Tru64 UNIX and
WinNT/Win2000
Communicate clearly complex technical concepts both in a written and
an oral manner

Experience and Educational Requirements
Bachelors' degree in Computer Science is preferred
Minimum three years of systems support experience
Any combination of experience and training which provides the
preferred knowledge, skills, and abilities may be acceptable
Must have good organizational skills and strong verbal and written
communication skills.
Must have the ability to set priorities, plan/organize, and carry out
installations and user support in an efficient manner
Capable of lifting 50 pounds
Minimum 2 years strong Unix and Windows NT administration experience,
to include Tru64
Solid understanding of networking/distributed computing, including
TCP/IP services, TruCluster, LAN/WAN routing, VPN, and network
topology
Server development experience
Distributed systems experience
Shell scripting or programming experience
Team attitude and strong communication skills
necessary

Come work with me...

